.TH NETMON 1 "2026-10-10" "netmon.sh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netmon \- take one WAN health sample for the netmon timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netmon.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netmon.sh
takes one WAN/mesh health sample and appends a TSV line to
.IR ~/.cache/netmon.log .
Normally run by a systemd user timer every 5 minutes; takes no arguments.
.P
Each run pings the gateway (192.168.0.1), Cloudflare (1.1.1.1), and Quad9
(9.9.9.9) with 4 probes, then measures download speed against two Arch
mirrors in parallel (8 s cap each) and logs loss/avg/max plus Mbps columns.
Columns: ts gw_loss gw_avg gw_max cf_loss cf_avg cf_max q9_loss q9_avg q9_max
spdA_mbps spdB_mbps agg_mbps.
.SH OPTIONS
None. Takes no flags or arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Take one manual sample:
.IP
.EX
netmon.sh
tail \-n 5 ~/.cache/netmon.log
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Sample appended (failed probes log as 100% loss, not as an error).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/netmon.log
Append-only TSV log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (8),
.BR curl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
